{"id":"src/lib/nl2sql/eval/selftest.ts","pkg":"src/lib/nl2sql","kind":"module","lines":1814,"commentLines":116,"header":["This file holds everything about the natural-language-to-SQL experiment that I can prove WITHOUT a live language model. It runs against a scratch local PostgreSQL (never your real database): NL2SQL_TEST_ADMIN_URL=postgres://postgres:pw@127.0.0.1:5432/postgres \\ npx tsx src/lib/nl2sql/eval/selftest.ts What it proves: the SQL guard, the database-level read-only security, the phonetic building blocks against the app's existing JavaScript engine, the prompt, the repair loop, logging and tick/cross, and -- with a stand-in \"model\" that replies with the reference SQL -- that every golden question runs through the full pipeline and matches. What it CANNOT prove is how well the REAL model writes SQL from new wordings; for that I use run-live.ts."],"symbols":[{"name":"ADMIN_URL","kind":"constant","exported":false,"line":54,"sig":"const ADMIN_URL = process.env.NL2SQL_TEST_ADMIN_URL || \"postgres://postgres:pw@127.0.0.1:5432/postgres\"","type":"","doc":[],"members":[],"items":0,"id":"26d0fd384e-ADMIN_URL","usedBy":[]},{"name":"TEST_DB","kind":"constant","exported":false,"line":55,"sig":"const TEST_DB = \"nl2sql_selftest\"","type":"","doc":[],"members":[],"items":0,"id":"26d0fd384e-TEST_DB","usedBy":[]},{"name":"SQL_DIR","kind":"constant","exported":false,"line":56,"sig":"const SQL_DIR = join(__dirname, \"..\", \"sql\")","type":"","doc":[],"members":[],"items":0,"id":"26d0fd384e-SQL_DIR","usedBy":[]},{"name":"passed","kind":"constant","exported":false,"line":58,"sig":"let passed = 0","type":"","doc":[],"members":[],"items":0,"id":"26d0fd384e-passed","usedBy":[]},{"name":"failed","kind":"constant","exported":false,"line":59,"sig":"let failed = 0","type":"","doc":[],"members":[],"items":0,"id":"26d0fd384e-failed","usedBy":[]},{"name":"failures","kind":"constant","exported":false,"line":60,"sig":"const failures: string[] = []","type":"string[]","doc":[],"memb